  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">SYR005N Syria Joint Response III</narrative>
  </title>
  <description promeva:title="Description (English)" promeva:type="104" type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">CARE is implementing a FSL and Protection project in Idlib province, targeting IDPs and host communities that have been affected by the conflict in  Syria, including vulnerable families that have fled the fighting in Aleppo. The  food security component includes cash/vouchers, support to the agriculture process of producing wheat through material inputs and support; and support to livestock through vaccination campaigns and provision of fodder. The project is innovative as it purchases wheat directly from farmers at a good price, enables for safe storage, then re-selling at better price and/or direct distributions to families who are unable to purchase bread/food. The Protection component of the project entails outreach and monitoring. A component of the project is implemented with 4 additional consortium partners, for a holistic &#x201C;full package&#x201D; response to vulnerable households.</narrative>
  </description>
